# Existing Behavior Preservation Contract

Treat all existing functionality as **protected by default**. Implement only the requested change with the **smallest possible change surface**.

## Golden Rule

The app is stable and working. Success = requested change **plus** all unrelated behavior unchanged. Do not improve, refactor, modernize, simplify, or redesign unless explicitly asked.

## Preserve Unless Explicitly Requested

Do **not** change: business logic, API contracts/payloads, DB/schema, validation, state, routing, authz, error/loading/success states, input/gesture behavior, responsive/a11y behavior, styling/layout (unless part of the request), or remove “unused” features.

If it works and the task does not ask to change it → **leave it alone**.

## No Unrequested Refactoring

Do not use the task to: refactor nearby code, rename unrelated symbols/files, change architecture, swap libraries, upgrade packages, rewrite working components, convert patterns, clean unrelated debt, reformat large areas, or add abstractions when existing ones suffice.

## Preserve Interfaces

Treat signatures, props, events, API/DB formats, URL/query params, storage shapes, CSS class contracts, and shared component behavior as **contracts**. Change them only when the request requires it; call out necessary breaks and minimize impact.

## Understand Before Editing

Inspect implementation and call sites; know what must change vs stay. Prefer extend over rewrite. Never start by rewriting a working component from scratch.

## Scope Strictly

Change only what satisfies the request. Prefer: one component over five; CSS over JS when enough; local over shared/global; extend over replace.

## Do Not Guess Intent

If interpretations could disturb existing behavior → **ask**. Do not “fix” or add product/UX decisions that were not requested. Existing behavior is intentional unless proven broken or the task asks to change it.

## Regression & Scope Boundaries

- Before coding: state **requested change**, **protected behavior**, and **expected files**.
- Prefer the option with fewer files/lines/deps/side effects, reuse, easy revert.
- Validate per `no-regressions-clean-edits` / `code-quality-validation`. Fix regressions you caused; do not delete tests to pass.
- Pre-existing unrelated bugs: **report**, do not silently expand scope.

```text
❌ BAD — feature needs a button; also renames helpers, restyles the page, “cleans” nearby hooks
✅ GOOD — add the button and the minimal wiring; leave everything else untouched
```
